Curses for OS9/68000 (tested under 2.1 and 2.2)===============================================This Curses-Package is derived from the ncurses-lib by Pavel Curtis.Its mainly a port (and several bugfixes) with one fundamental change:It uses TERMCAP instead of TERMINFO  !!!(a terminfo version was running, but was discarded since OSK don'tknow terminfo.)The Programmer can neglect this change totally, because theinitialisation routines parses and interprets the termcap entry alone(i.e.  you don't need to link termlib.l) and completely (i.e. notget{num,flag,str}() calls are needed ...). This implies that the meaning of all existing termcap identifiers areknown at compile-time. Please edit the Table in the File lib_tcutils.cto reflect all known termcap-identifiers (the table must be sorted !).Therefore this library looks to the programmer like a SYSV-Curseswithout Pads.The name 'ncurses' was choosen since a.) that was the name of the original lib.b.) microware has already a 'normal' curses-lib (delivered with the    SSM-Module (??).Ncurses has several advantages over the curses-lib from microware:	- its more complete (no pads though)	- its faster (a lot !)	- no fiddling with PC_,BC,UP and termlib.l is neccessary	- you have the Source-code :-)Disadvantages:	- its bigger	- the meaning of the termcap identifiers are fixed and static          (but you have the source ... so ??)I hope you can use this library ....	Reimer MellinUUCP: ram@altger.UUCP